<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Steiff</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1880">1880</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Margarete Steiff GmbH</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Steiff is a German toy company based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giengen-an-der-brenz">Giengen an der Brenz</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margarete-steiff">Margarete Steiff</a> in 1880. It is best known for its plush teddy bears, first made in the early 1900s, which carry its trademark button in the ear. The company has remained in the hands of the Steiff family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/steiff.jpg" alt="Steiff" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steiffmargarete.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
